==Trivia== 
*Dyle's name is a pun on the word 'Dial' and maybe on the male name 'Kyle', and his last name (Timesly) is a pun on the word 'Time' or 'Timely'. 
**His name also sounds like the world 'Dial', which could resemble the fact he is a clock.
*His name in old English means secret or hidden, which would make sense since he isn't in the show but rather a secret [[Toon]] who operates the trains.
*As stated in his {{CI|Twisted Dyle}}[[Twisted Dyle|Twisted counterpart]]'s description and implied in his [[Gossip]] about {{CI|Sprout|name=true}}, Dyle was the only [[Toon]] who saw the outside world, and the only one who had access to the train that left [[Gardenview]]. No other Toon had access to that specific train.
*Dyle is the second {{Type|Lethal}} [[Toon]] since {{CI|Dandy|name=true}}, who was added upon release, appearing almost 14 months after [[Dandy's World]] was released.
*Dyle's designation number is OA-001, with the "OA" most likely standing for Operational Assistant, but he is still in the Lethal category.
**This makes sense as he has no role in the [[show]], operating the trains instead.
**It could also stand for "Off-Air" since he wasn't intended to be put in the show, according to a radio transcript.
*According to Dyle's [[Gossip]] about {{CI|Scraps|name=true}}, his animal preferences are ponies.
**Because of this, there is a common belief that Dyle is a fan of {{wp|My Little Pony}}, albeit it's not directly said or confirmed.
***When asked in the Third YouTube Livestream, [[Qwel]] stated she wasn't brave enough to give an answer for if Dyle likes My Little Pony.
***In the "It Was All a Dream 💤" video, a music box version of the intro theme of My Little Pony can be heard, meaning Dyle does know My Little Pony.
*Dyle is one of the two un-playable [[Toons]], with the other being [[Dandy]].
**If we consider other Minor Toons like {{CI|Blot Jr.|name=true}} and {{CI|Barnaby|name=true}}, that number rises to 4. While he and Dandy aren't playable to regular users, the minor Toons aren't playable at all.
*Dyle has a hatred towards {{CI|Shrimpo|name=true}}, to the point where he sometimes conspires about removing him from Gardenview, making him the only [[Toon]] to actually bear a true grudge against Shrimpo, and not just viewing him as annoying.
**In the "It Was All a Dream 💤" video, Dyle is shown dreaming about running Shrimpo over with a train, which further proves that he has a desire to take Shrimpo's life.
*Dyle is the first [[Toon]] to wear shoes/footwear in his default [[Skin]], the second being {{CI|Soulvester|name=true}}, and the third being {{CI|Waxwell|name=true}}.
*Dyle is the first male [[Toon]] to have eyeshadow in his default [[Skin]].
*Dyle is the first [[Toon]] with any semblance of facial hair in his default [[Skin]], as well as the first character to alongside his  [[Twisted Dyle|Twisted counterpart]].
*Dyle does not like physical contact, especially when unpermitted. This makes it hard to be around {{CI|Goob|name=true}} because of his spontaneous hugging.
*Dyle may have a fear and/or dislike of snakes, based on his gossip about {{CI|Teagan|name=true}}.
**It could also be a reference to the 2006 movie {{wp|Snakes on a Train}}.
**[[Twisted Dyle]] possesses a snake tail and sounds, suggesting the [[Ichor]] forced him to get past his fear.
*Despite also investigating and recordkeeping, Dyle isn't allowed to speak with {{CI|Rodger|name=true}} for reasons that have yet to be specified.
**This could possibly be due to the fact they'd likely talk a lot, distracting Dyle from his work, or Dyle might end up talking about the outside to Rodger, which, if the info is spread, could make the other Toons curious and vulnerable.
*Dyle is likely the [[Toon]] that gives [[Dandy]] [[Items]] for his [[Elevator]] Shop, as Dyle would have been the only one able to even get Items outside.
*Dyle is inspired by Tony the Talking Clock from [[w:c:donthugme|Don't Hug Me I'm Scared]], as stated in a livestream, similar to how {{CI|Glisten|name=true}} was an OC for it.
*{{CI|Looey|name=true}}, {{CI|Brightney|name=true}}, and {{CI|Pebble|name=true}} are the only [[Toons]] that Dyle doesn't mention by name in his [[gossips]], but contextual clues make it obvious to whom the Gossip is about.
**In fact, Looey and Brightney's gossips do not refer to them at all, but rather the groups they're leaders of, that being the Circus Troupe and the Book Club respectively.
*He is the second character to call Dandy by his real first name, Dandicus, with [[Teagan]] being the first.
*Dyle is the first shopkeeper to not have himself be purchasable in his shop (unless his [[Sticker]] is counted).
**Although [[Dandy]] doesn't seem to, developers are able to buy him in his shop, as he has a purchase dialogue seen within the game's code.
*Dyle is the only Lethal who doesn't have a [[Toon Handler]], although whether it's a coincidence or not; {{CI|Delilah|name=true}} seem to wear similar pants, and his name has the first syllable of her name, similar to the Toon Handlers with their respective Toons.
*One of Dyle's gossip faces uses his hurt face texture, like how [[Dandy]]'s hurt face is his third stage of no buying.
**This could imply that {{Type|Lethals}}' hurt faces are similar to their face textures in different parts of the game.
*Dyle is the first and only [[Toon]] with a full name to willingly reveal it, doing so when gossiping about {{CI|Brusha|name=true}} and {{CI|Razzle & Dazzle|name=true}}.
*[[Dandy]] and Dyle are similar in several ways;
**Their [[Twisted]] counterparts are {{Type|Lethals}}.
**They own a store in the [[lobby]].
**Their [[Toon]] counterparts are unplayable by the general public.
**They have rainbow colors in their designs (though Dyle has violet while Dandy doesn't).
***Dyle's color scheme is the only appearance of a 7-colored rainbow in the game.
**They are the first and only Toon in their designations, OA and L.
**They are both male toons.
**Their names (and [[Dazzle]]'s) start with D.
**They share similar [[Abilities]], with them being Passives, similar formatting and having the same description.
***Due to sharing Abilities, Dyle's Ability reads "The star of the [[show]]," despite him having no in-show role.
*The lever Dyle pulls on his stand controls when the train stops in the [[Lobby]].
*Dyle is tied with {{CI|Vee|name=true}} for having the shortest full names, with both having 11 letters.
**However, when including spaces, Dyle has the shortest full name with 12 characters as Vee's full name includes 2 spaces.
*In "Downtime with Dyle ⏱️ | Dandy's World Animation", Dyle can be seen with red dots in his eyes and a fang sticking out of his mouth out of annoyance, which could mean Dyle can turn into [[Twisted Dyle]] when he gets angry. Unlike Dandy, he seems to be able to turn back into a [[Toon]] and control his anger, showing higher self-control than Dandy.
**Both the animation and [[Dyle's Floor|his in-game room]] also reveal he owns a white flip-phone.
*In Dyle's [[Gossip]] about {{CI|Cosmo|name=true}}, his dialogue text misspells the word delectable, spelling "delictable" instead. This may be a reference to {{CI|Sprout|name=true}} and Cosmo's dialogue and one of the posters found in-game, as the spelling will never be corrected.
*If you look at where the arrows point, Dyle's clock face appears to always read 4:38.
**However, the bottom of the arrows aren't in the middle, so actually reading it with angles would be hard.
*Dyle is the one to make the [[Event]]-exclusive [[Items]], with [[Dandy]] making him do it, as said by his dialogue in the [[Elevator]] when you take them.
**It also shows he can bake, paint eggs, and make candy, therefore being able to create the {{II|Christmas Cookie|name=false}}, {{II|Dandy Easter Egg|name=false}} and {{II|Dandy Corn|name=false}}.
***It is not specified whether Dyle made the Dandy Corn from scratch, or if it was delivered from the outside in some way.
*Despite Dyle having 5 Star Skill Check. his Skill Check Size is actually 120 in his code, with the true size being another Skill Check Size variant.<ref>[[File:Dyle Skill Check Size.png|thumb]]</ref>
*While being shown to use a security system in the "It Was All a Dream 💤" video, it's merely within a dream, and Dyle doesn't actually seem to use it at the end of the video. This is also shown in-game in [[Brusha]]'s lore video, where she reacts with surprise and curiosity after noticing a camera's still on, as well as the thought of someone still using the security system.
*Dyle and {{CI|Waxwell|name=true}} are the only [[Toons]] whose teeth can change from being flat and sharp, as seen in the Downtime with Dyle animation and his [[Halloween]] [[Skin]] (although they could be fake fangs).
*Weirdly enough, Dyle's [[Halloween]] [[Skin]] has no blink or hurt face.

